Don't worry about the magical armor unless it's speed or jumping
boots, because it's *really* hard to get good armor via polypiling.
Scrolls, potions, and rings are the biggies. Furthermore, there's
armor and guaranteed dragons at the castle (and at Ludios). So check
for what you need at the castle before you painstakingly polypile
armor. Oh, and *blessed fixed GREASED darts* was a typo - never grease
projectiles, or they'll slip when thrown.

Since you have magic resistance and several of the elemental
resistances, you're ready for the castle.



